  "solution": {
    "text": "Option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is theorem hence <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equivalent to <math><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> means only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> or only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math><br />Which is same as <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Means&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> happens but <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> does not happen. It means only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> or only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> happens<br />Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math><br />but not equivalent to <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>"
